concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Dissolution of Assembly by Governor-General"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If, in the opinion of the Governor-General, the Assembly: (a) is incapable of effectively performing its functions; or (b) is conducting its affairs in a grossly improper manner; the Governor-General may dissolve the Assembly. (2) Where the Assembly is dissolved: (a) the Governor-General: (i) shall appoint a Commissioner for the purposes of this section; and (ii) may, at any time, give directions to the Commissioner about the exercise of the powers of the Executive; and (b) a general election shall be held on a day specified by the Commonwealth Minister by notice published in the" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If, in the opinion of the Governor-General, the Assembly: (a) is incapable of effectively performing its functions; or (b) is conducting its affairs in a grossly improper manner; the Governor-General may dissolve the Assembly. (2) Where the Assembly is dissolved: (a) the Governor-General: (i) shall appoint a Commissioner for the purposes of this section; and (ii) may, at any time, give directions to the Commissioner about the exercise of the powers of the Executive; and (b) a general election shall be held on a day specified by the Commonwealth Minister by notice published in the"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d20e2edb5f95b44c2338198a6d44ba26c7bce1d390aebe09b98075d022af7484" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
