concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-21 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21 Standing rules and orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-21 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this Act, the Assembly may make standing rules and orders with respect to the conduct of business. (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), standing rules and orders may be made: (a) for the election of a deputy (however titled) to the Presiding Officer; and   Legislative Assembly  Part III Procedure of Assembly  Division 2 Section 21 Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (b) conferring on that deputy such powers as are specified in the rules and orders (including powers of the Presiding Officer under this Act)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to this Act, the Assembly may make standing rules and orders with respect to the conduct of business. (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), standing rules and orders may be made: (a) for the election of a deputy (however titled) to the Presiding Officer; and   Legislative Assembly  Part III Procedure of Assembly  Division 2 Section 21 Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (b) conferring on that deputy such powers as are specified in the rules and orders (including powers of the Presiding Officer under this Act)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d3f9a8b7497fb5bf97fa40261d4bd286a7f8a68c1662817881434d5769829871" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
