concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-65 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "65 Proposal of money votes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-65 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An enactment, vote or resolution (proposal) for the appropriation of the public money of the Territory must not be proposed in the Assembly except by a Minister. (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a member other than a Minister from moving an amendment to a proposal made by a Minister unless the amendment is to increase the amount of public money of the Territory to be appropriated." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An enactment, vote or resolution (proposal) for the appropriation of the public money of the Territory must not be proposed in the Assembly except by a Minister. (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent a member other than a Minister from moving an amendment to a proposal made by a Minister unless the amendment is to increase the amount of public money of the Territory to be appropriated."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9f5347882bb90756bb509c249704003492253bc9b1259426ce702810e18b9222" ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer ;
