concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-69a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69A Acts that bind States to bind Territory"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-69a ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an Act (whether or not by express provision) binds each of the States, or the Crown in right of each of the States, that Act binds the Territory, or the Crown in right of the Territory, by force of this subsection, unless that Act specifically provides otherwise. (2) Subsection (1) does not affect the application of a law of the Commonwealth in and in relation to the Territory otherwise than as provided in that subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an Act (whether or not by express provision) binds each of the States, or the Crown in right of each of the States, that Act binds the Territory, or the Crown in right of the Territory, by force of this subsection, unless that Act specifically provides otherwise. (2) Subsection (1) does not affect the application of a law of the Commonwealth in and in relation to the Territory otherwise than as provided in that subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9240dc63a82041514dc492ff7bd63e16ef91a62270f0a2544d54021b32797b26" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-69a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-self-government-act-1988-sch-5-sec-69a-ss-2 ;
